      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the middle-ware filters, shouldn\u0027t we be leveraging the service\u0027s native logger?\n\ndef get_logger(conf, service\u003dNone):\n    logger \u003d None\n    log_name \u003d \u0027keystone.middleware\u0027\n    if service:\n        if service \u003d\u003d \u0027swift\u0027:\n            try:\n                from swift.common.utils import get_logger\n                logger \u003d get_logger(conf, log_route\u003dlog_name)\n            except:\n                # unable to get the swift logger\n                # will create a default one later\n                pass\n        elif service \u003d\u003d \u0027nova\u0027:\n            try:\n                from nova import log as logging\n                logger \u003d logging.getLogger(log_name)\n            except:\n                # unable to get the nova logger\n                # will create a default later\n                pass\n        \n            # use default one\n    if not logger:\n            try:\n                logger \u003d logging.getLogger(log_name)\n            except:\n                # shouldn\u0027t happen, but what can we do?\n                pass\n\n    return logger",
      "revId": "eba50d6750a13f2bcb7500b42030582803ae2fd2",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
